1
00:00:05,133 --> 00:00:11,933
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,833 --> 00:00:32,800
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:34,167 --> 00:00:35,300
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:40,300 --> 00:00:41,567
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,467 --> 00:00:43,967
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:44,100 --> 00:00:45,133
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,267 --> 00:00:46,467
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:47,167 --> 00:00:48,733
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:50,867 --> 00:00:51,933
[GUNSHOT]

10
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:53,667
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:54,500 --> 00:00:56,267
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,833 --> 00:00:57,800
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:59,133 --> 00:01:00,600
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:01,267 --> 00:01:02,833
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:05,367 --> 00:01:06,600
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:08,367 --> 00:01:09,500
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:10,367 --> 00:01:11,667
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:11,800 --> 00:01:13,300
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:13,400 --> 00:01:15,833
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:20,067 --> 00:01:22,033
<i> If not for my men,</i>

21
00:01:22,167 --> 00:01:23,667
<i> Victor Zafra would've escaped.</i>

22
00:01:23,867 --> 00:01:26,633
<i>Don't you think it'll be
quicker if we both act on it?</i>

23
00:01:26,800 --> 00:01:28,500
<i>We don't need to disclose
all our information.</i>

24
00:01:28,633 --> 00:01:30,200
Tuazon, that's not coordination.

25
00:01:30,333 --> 00:01:31,600
<i> That is control.</i>

26
00:01:31,700 --> 00:01:32,967
<i> And someone has to have it.</i>

27
00:01:33,133 --> 00:01:34,300
<i> And that's me.</i>

28
00:01:34,467 --> 00:01:37,367
<i>We already gave you
75 million pesos.</i>

29
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:39,933
<i> You are their only suspect.</i>

30
00:01:40,033 --> 00:01:43,433
<i>But what matters is there's
no evidence tied back to you.</i>

31
00:01:43,600 --> 00:01:45,533
<i> But the moment you cross us,</i>

32
00:01:45,667 --> 00:01:47,667
<i>you won't have time
to regret it.</i>

33
00:01:47,833 --> 00:01:50,567
<i>But I was wondering if I could
take tomorrow off.</i>

34
00:01:50,700 --> 00:01:52,800
<i>- It's Rudy's birthday.
- Fine.</i>

35
00:01:52,933 --> 00:01:54,400
<i>And you think
you'll win Betchay over?</i>

36
00:01:54,533 --> 00:01:57,167
<i> I can get whatever I want.</i>

37
00:01:57,333 --> 00:01:58,367
<i> When we got here,</i>

38
00:01:58,500 --> 00:02:01,067
<i>we found her
fixing up the house.</i>

39
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:02,567
<i> Happy birthday, by the way.</i>

40
00:02:02,700 --> 00:02:03,900
<i>- Oh!
- That's right!</i>

41
00:02:04,033 --> 00:02:05,500
<i>- It's my birthday!
- Your birthday!</i>

42
00:02:05,667 --> 00:02:07,467
<i>I almost forgot.
Thank you.</i>

43
00:02:07,600 --> 00:02:09,967
<i>When are you going
to tell her the truth?</i>

44
00:02:10,100 --> 00:02:11,800
<i> Until I'm certain she's safe,</i>

45
00:02:11,900 --> 00:02:13,533
<i>she'll have to stay
in our house.</i>

46
00:02:13,700 --> 00:02:16,267
<i>Maybe she overheard
how Betchay put us down.</i>

47
00:02:16,400 --> 00:02:18,167
<i>If Auntie Betchay did that
to Gloria,</i>

48
00:02:18,267 --> 00:02:19,833
<i> we'd have a real problem.</i>

49
00:02:20,967 --> 00:02:21,933
Ma'am?

50
00:02:25,767 --> 00:02:27,600
Breakfast, ma'am.

51
00:02:27,600 --> 00:02:30,100
I went to your room,
but you were here.

52
00:02:34,100 --> 00:02:35,867
You spent the whole night
thinking

53
00:02:35,867 --> 00:02:37,100
about Ma'am Sam, didn't you?

54
00:02:37,433 --> 00:02:38,367
[SIGHS]

55
00:02:38,467 --> 00:02:40,233
Toto and I did, too.

56
00:02:40,367 --> 00:02:42,200
But like they say...

57
00:02:43,067 --> 00:02:45,833
Where there's life,
there's hope.

58
00:02:45,933 --> 00:02:47,200
But what if...

59
00:02:49,733 --> 00:02:52,033
[VOICE BREAKS]
Sam's already dead?

60
00:02:52,133 --> 00:02:53,567
We don't even know

61
00:02:53,667 --> 00:02:55,700
what really happened
to Ma'am Sam.

62
00:02:56,100 --> 00:02:58,067
And I don't think it'll help

63
00:02:58,167 --> 00:03:00,033
if you keep thinking negatively.

64
00:03:00,133 --> 00:03:01,933
Ma'am, isn't Ma'am Sam tough?

65
00:03:02,267 --> 00:03:05,567
She could take on
an entire battalion of enemies

66
00:03:05,733 --> 00:03:07,167
and handle them
like it's nothing.

67
00:03:07,167 --> 00:03:08,867
Ma'am Sam's a survivor.

68
00:03:09,500 --> 00:03:11,300
So please, don't worry, ma'am.

69
00:03:11,467 --> 00:03:13,133
Thank you, Twinkle.

70
00:03:14,933 --> 00:03:17,400
But I'm sorry.
Your concern and your words

71
00:03:17,500 --> 00:03:19,633
aren't enough to put me at ease.

72
00:03:21,667 --> 00:03:23,500
There's only one thing
that can do that.

73
00:03:26,500 --> 00:03:28,733
When Sam comes home to us.

74
00:03:29,167 --> 00:03:31,133
[ISOBEL SOBBING]

75
00:03:31,267 --> 00:03:34,833
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

76
00:03:36,667 --> 00:03:40,300
Wow, you really bought
a lot of ingredients!

77
00:03:40,433 --> 00:03:41,467
What are you planning to cook?

78
00:03:41,600 --> 00:03:42,500
Uh, Papa.

79
00:03:42,667 --> 00:03:44,767
Gloria said last night

80
00:03:44,867 --> 00:03:47,900
that she wanted to cook
something for your birthday.

81
00:03:48,500 --> 00:03:50,500
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

82
00:03:50,667 --> 00:03:52,733
Papa, happy birthday again.

83
00:03:53,833 --> 00:03:56,767
- [GABO GIGGLES]
- Thank you, son.

84
00:03:57,567 --> 00:04:00,033
We really should celebrate
your birthday.

85
00:04:00,167 --> 00:04:02,000
It's also a way of thanking God.

86
00:04:02,133 --> 00:04:03,200
Thank you very much.

87
00:04:03,367 --> 00:04:05,700
So, Gloria?
Should I cook all of this?

88
00:04:06,400 --> 00:04:08,000
Auntie, that's what
I was hoping to ask.

89
00:04:08,133 --> 00:04:10,300
Could you teach me first?

90
00:04:10,400 --> 00:04:11,867
I still can't remember
how to cook.

91
00:04:12,033 --> 00:04:12,967
Honey, don't.

92
00:04:13,167 --> 00:04:15,667
I'll cook instead.
I don't want you to get tired.

93
00:04:15,667 --> 00:04:16,500
Aunty and I can do it.

94
00:04:16,633 --> 00:04:17,867
- Yeah.
- No, I'll do it.

95
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:19,800
It's for Papa Rudy's birthday,
after all.

96
00:04:20,533 --> 00:04:22,500
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

97
00:04:22,667 --> 00:04:24,000
Before we start,

98
00:04:24,133 --> 00:04:25,667
I'm just going to use
the bathroom.

99
00:04:25,800 --> 00:04:27,967
- Oh, sure. Go ahead.
- Wait, honey.

100
00:04:28,200 --> 00:04:29,333
- Uncle?
- Yes?

101
00:04:29,600 --> 00:04:30,733
Is there water
in the bathroom?

102
00:04:30,900 --> 00:04:32,200
Yes, I just fetched some.

103
00:04:32,767 --> 00:04:34,700
Come on, honey.
I'll go with you.

104
00:04:36,067 --> 00:04:38,900
- I wonder what she bought.
- Let me see.

105
00:04:43,067 --> 00:04:44,333
This one. There!

106
00:04:44,433 --> 00:04:46,900
The third one! That's it!

107
00:04:47,033 --> 00:04:47,900
There you go.

108
00:04:48,033 --> 00:04:50,267
- I'll just take this one, miss.
- Okay, ma'am.

109
00:04:50,267 --> 00:04:52,700
- You can pay at the cashier.
- Oh, okay.

110
00:04:53,100 --> 00:04:54,333
How much is it, Miss?

111
00:04:54,433 --> 00:04:55,733
- 1,500 pesos.
- 1,500?

112
00:04:58,567 --> 00:05:00,833
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

113
00:05:00,967 --> 00:05:03,067
I've only got 1,000.
Can you give me a discount?

114
00:05:03,200 --> 00:05:04,733
I'm sorry,
we can't give discounts.

115
00:05:04,900 --> 00:05:06,933
Come on.
It's for good luck.

116
00:05:07,033 --> 00:05:09,733
I'm giving it to my husband.
It's his birthday today.

117
00:05:09,967 --> 00:05:11,400
- Please.
- I'm really sorry.

118
00:05:11,400 --> 00:05:13,233
- Betchay.
- Hey.

119
00:05:13,300 --> 00:05:14,600
What are you doing here?

120
00:05:14,600 --> 00:05:17,867
I'm following you around
in case you need anything.

121
00:05:17,867 --> 00:05:19,233
- Like this.
- No...

122
00:05:19,600 --> 00:05:20,900
No, no, wait!

123
00:05:21,100 --> 00:05:22,600
You're following me around

124
00:05:22,733 --> 00:05:25,000
just so you can pay
for Rudy's gift?!

125
00:05:25,100 --> 00:05:27,367
Just consider it a loan.

126
00:05:27,467 --> 00:05:30,767
When you have the money,
you can pay me back.

127
00:05:32,900 --> 00:05:34,900
Come on. Take it.

128
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:39,133
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

129
00:05:39,300 --> 00:05:41,467
- Here you go, ma'am.
- Thank you.

130
00:05:42,233 --> 00:05:43,900
Why won't you give me
a discount?

131
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:45,267
I said it's for good luck.

132
00:05:45,400 --> 00:05:47,133
- Betchay?
- Yes?

133
00:05:47,300 --> 00:05:48,267
Wait a minute.

134
00:05:49,433 --> 00:05:50,733
I'm taking you shopping.

135
00:05:50,833 --> 00:05:53,600
- Pick whatever you want.
- Good grief!

136
00:05:53,733 --> 00:05:56,033
That's way too much, Paquito!

137
00:05:56,667 --> 00:05:57,800
You're doing too much.

138
00:05:57,933 --> 00:05:59,767
It's not too much.

139
00:05:59,900 --> 00:06:02,800
You'll be using these
as the manager of BeerGin.

140
00:06:04,067 --> 00:06:07,567
Anything you want,
anything you like,

141
00:06:07,700 --> 00:06:09,667
anything that fits you,
take it.

142
00:06:09,800 --> 00:06:11,300
Anything?

143
00:06:11,633 --> 00:06:12,733
I'll take care of you.

144
00:06:12,867 --> 00:06:19,833
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

145
00:06:21,267 --> 00:06:23,167
How about this?
Do you like it?

146
00:06:24,033 --> 00:06:25,833
It looks perfect on you.

147
00:06:25,967 --> 00:06:33,067
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

148
00:06:36,100 --> 00:06:37,800
Red looks good on you.

149
00:06:37,933 --> 00:06:39,300
How about this?

150
00:06:39,433 --> 00:06:40,400
Do you like it?

151
00:06:40,533 --> 00:06:42,000
Why? Do I smell bad already?

152
00:06:42,200 --> 00:06:43,467
Not at all.

153
00:06:43,700 --> 00:06:47,267
I just want your scent
to stand out in the bar.

154
00:06:47,367 --> 00:06:48,800
[BETCHAY SCOFFS]

155
00:06:48,800 --> 00:06:51,200
I guess I don't want to smell
like all the other girls

156
00:06:51,200 --> 00:06:53,000
- at the bar.
- [PAQUITO CHUCKLES]

157
00:06:54,800 --> 00:06:56,500
[BETCHAY SQUEALS, GIGGLES]

158
00:06:56,667 --> 00:06:57,967
Wait! [GIGGLING]

159
00:06:58,900 --> 00:07:00,433
Should we buy it?

160
00:07:00,733 --> 00:07:02,700
No. You've already
bought me too much.

161
00:07:02,867 --> 00:07:04,000
It's way too expensive.

162
00:07:04,133 --> 00:07:05,367
[CHUCKLES]

163
00:07:05,500 --> 00:07:08,200
- You know, Betchay...
- Oh, what?

164
00:07:10,033 --> 00:07:13,000
Don't tell me
you're in love with me.

165
00:07:13,133 --> 00:07:16,000
Fine, then.
I won't say I love...

166
00:07:16,167 --> 00:07:17,200
Stop!

167
00:07:17,333 --> 00:07:20,400
[BOTH CHUCKLING]

168
00:07:20,567 --> 00:07:21,533
Come on.

169
00:07:21,667 --> 00:07:22,900
Ma'am, are you ready to pay?

170
00:07:23,067 --> 00:07:24,400
- He's paying.
- Okay.

171
00:07:24,567 --> 00:07:26,000
We'll just go to the cashier.

172
00:07:28,033 --> 00:07:31,200
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

173
00:07:31,333 --> 00:07:33,133
- How much is everything?
- 3,000 pesos.

174
00:07:33,500 --> 00:07:34,833
What? Are you sure?

175
00:07:34,933 --> 00:07:36,533
- Yes, I am!
- You saw them?

176
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:39,233
And that Betchay...

177
00:07:39,400 --> 00:07:41,567
The way she keeps clinging
to your husband, my God!

178
00:07:41,733 --> 00:07:43,067
She's like a leech!

179
00:07:43,233 --> 00:07:45,167
Those two are really
trying me.

180
00:07:45,267 --> 00:07:48,500
But don't tell Boss Paquito
that I told you, okay?

181
00:07:48,633 --> 00:07:51,267
I don't care!
I'll deal with him!

182
00:07:51,900 --> 00:07:53,867
She still hasn't learned
her lesson, huh?

183
00:07:54,067 --> 00:07:55,300
I already slapped her.

184
00:07:55,300 --> 00:07:56,933
Well, she's just too flirty.

185
00:07:57,133 --> 00:07:58,033
She'll never learn.

186
00:08:06,233 --> 00:08:09,700
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

187
00:08:09,800 --> 00:08:13,233
[SAM]<i> If I have to pretend
</i> I'm part of their family,

188
00:08:13,600 --> 00:08:14,867
<i> I'll do it.</i>

189
00:08:15,400 --> 00:08:17,767
<i>I'll let them get used
to having me around.</i>

190
00:08:18,900 --> 00:08:20,767
<i>Until they feel comfortable
with me</i>

191
00:08:21,300 --> 00:08:23,133
<i> and completely trust me.</i>

192
00:08:24,500 --> 00:08:26,400
<i> Once I have their trust,</i>

193
00:08:27,267 --> 00:08:30,233
<i>I'll have more freedom to
move around and investigate.</i>

194
00:08:30,400 --> 00:08:32,900
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

195
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:39,567
- Pa.
- Oh?

196
00:08:39,567 --> 00:08:41,600
Looks like we're going
to have a good day today.

197
00:08:41,600 --> 00:08:42,967
Tell me about it!

198
00:08:42,967 --> 00:08:44,733
Move! I said move!

199
00:08:44,733 --> 00:08:46,100
Hey, Paquito!

200
00:08:46,100 --> 00:08:47,833
Where have you been?
You went home in the morning.

201
00:08:47,833 --> 00:08:50,333
Where else?
At BeerGin, of course.

202
00:08:50,333 --> 00:08:52,500
This is the first time you've
stayed there until morning.

203
00:08:52,500 --> 00:08:54,067
- What's the occasion?
- Nothing.

204
00:08:54,100 --> 00:08:55,700
They said you were with Betchay.

205
00:08:55,700 --> 00:08:56,800
What did you two do?

206
00:08:56,800 --> 00:08:59,500
Spent hours together?
Went on a shopping spree?

207
00:08:59,500 --> 00:09:01,633
I know you too well.
I know your tricks.

208
00:09:01,633 --> 00:09:03,033
You do those things
to get a woman!

209
00:09:03,033 --> 00:09:05,500
What are you talking about?

210
00:09:05,500 --> 00:09:07,033
Someone saw you with her!

211
00:09:07,033 --> 00:09:08,500
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

212
00:09:08,500 --> 00:09:09,667
Hey, you!

213
00:09:09,667 --> 00:09:12,967
Matet, I went with Betchay

214
00:09:12,967 --> 00:09:15,767
to buy a gift for Rudy!

215
00:09:15,767 --> 00:09:17,633
Don't you dare
make up stories again.

216
00:09:18,433 --> 00:09:20,833
Or else you'll get hurt!

217
00:09:21,833 --> 00:09:23,833
And you, shut your mouth!

218
00:09:25,133 --> 00:09:27,100
[FOOTSTEPS RETREATING]

219
00:09:31,500 --> 00:09:33,800
[DJANGO] Nosy people...

220
00:09:33,800 --> 00:09:35,900
are truly digging
their own graves.

221
00:09:35,900 --> 00:09:37,733
[LAUGHS EVILLY]

222
00:09:37,733 --> 00:09:39,167
Matet!

223
00:09:39,167 --> 00:09:40,800
Matet might get killed.

224
00:09:40,800 --> 00:09:42,933
[LAUGHS EVILLY]

225
00:09:44,567 --> 00:09:46,767
Boss, agents from NLEA are here.

226
00:09:48,033 --> 00:09:49,033
Sir.

227
00:09:50,067 --> 00:09:51,633
- Sir.
- Domingo.

228
00:09:52,500 --> 00:09:53,600
Umali.

229
00:09:54,733 --> 00:09:57,533
- Any news?
- We're done with the task

230
00:09:57,533 --> 00:09:58,867
you asked regarding the Zafras.

231
00:09:58,867 --> 00:10:00,500
Good.

232
00:10:00,500 --> 00:10:01,967
Let's talk in my office.

233
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:03,400
Max, you might want to join us.

234
00:10:04,033 --> 00:10:09,000
- [FOOTSTEPS RETREATING]
- [PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

235
00:10:14,567 --> 00:10:17,533
Sir, we wanted
to talk to you personally

236
00:10:17,533 --> 00:10:21,867
to report this
very special case to you.

237
00:10:23,767 --> 00:10:25,033
What have you discovered?

238
00:10:25,033 --> 00:10:27,200
The Zafras are operating
business as usual.

239
00:10:27,200 --> 00:10:30,867
They continue delivering gold
to their clients.

240
00:10:30,867 --> 00:10:32,000
After what they did to me,

241
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:33,700
they didn't even think
for a second.

242
00:10:36,100 --> 00:10:38,767
They really think they can just
go back to their normal lives.

243
00:10:38,767 --> 00:10:42,233
Sir, they made a mistake
attacking you.

244
00:10:42,233 --> 00:10:45,767
General, what do you want us
to do next?

245
00:10:45,767 --> 00:10:46,967
We are ready.

246
00:10:46,967 --> 00:10:48,600
Raid their businesses.

247
00:10:48,600 --> 00:10:51,133
It's an open secret that they've
a lot of misdeclarations,

248
00:10:51,133 --> 00:10:54,233
and they violate a lot
of environmental regulations.

249
00:10:54,233 --> 00:10:56,767
When they see that the NLEA
is the lead agency,

250
00:10:56,767 --> 00:10:58,600
they'll know they won't be able
to get away.

251
00:10:58,600 --> 00:10:59,933
You can count on us, General.

252
00:11:00,867 --> 00:11:02,033
Don't let me down.

253
00:11:08,100 --> 00:11:09,200
Excuse me, Dad.

254
00:11:09,967 --> 00:11:11,100
The Zafras?

255
00:11:11,900 --> 00:11:13,767
That's the case
Sam was handling, right?

256
00:11:14,267 --> 00:11:16,833
Why are we focusing on them?

257
00:11:16,833 --> 00:11:18,767
Max, you'll have to trust me
on this.

258
00:11:22,133 --> 00:11:23,667
Dad.

259
00:11:23,667 --> 00:11:24,900
If you know something...

260
00:11:27,800 --> 00:11:29,633
you should've told us then.

261
00:11:29,633 --> 00:11:31,000
And Sam would've known.

262
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:33,467
If you did, we wouldn't be
dealing with this now.

263
00:11:34,133 --> 00:11:35,033
So please,

264
00:11:35,833 --> 00:11:36,900
please, Dad.

265
00:11:38,233 --> 00:11:39,567
Tell me.

266
00:11:39,567 --> 00:11:40,733
Tell me what you know.

267
00:11:43,100 --> 00:11:44,100
Lao!

268
00:11:44,100 --> 00:11:45,967
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

269
00:11:45,967 --> 00:11:47,633
- Boss.
- Have you spoken to the people

270
00:11:47,633 --> 00:11:49,833
who were with us
looking for Samantha's body?

271
00:11:49,833 --> 00:11:51,033
They haven't sent
any updates, boss.

272
00:11:51,033 --> 00:11:52,200
Tell them to go home!

273
00:11:52,200 --> 00:11:53,700
[LEE] Hold on, boss.

274
00:11:53,700 --> 00:11:55,133
What do you mean?

275
00:11:55,133 --> 00:11:57,333
We're going to stop searching
for Samantha Jacinto?

276
00:11:57,333 --> 00:11:58,667
No.

277
00:11:58,667 --> 00:12:00,267
We'll look for her ourselves.

278
00:12:00,267 --> 00:12:01,800
They're useless!

279
00:12:01,800 --> 00:12:04,167
- Stallone, get my gun!
- Okay, boss.

280
00:12:04,167 --> 00:12:05,833
Move!

281
00:12:05,833 --> 00:12:07,633
All of you, come with me!

282
00:12:10,633 --> 00:12:11,933
Lucas.

283
00:12:11,933 --> 00:12:13,967
Boys, hold, hold.

284
00:12:15,133 --> 00:12:16,133
Ma.

285
00:12:16,133 --> 00:12:18,333
I'll go back to where
I last saw Samantha.

286
00:12:19,200 --> 00:12:21,167
I'll make sure she's dead.

287
00:12:22,800 --> 00:12:24,667
With what happened
to your brother,

288
00:12:26,033 --> 00:12:29,000
for sure NCIA isn't
the only agency after us.

289
00:12:30,033 --> 00:12:31,033
There's NLEA.

290
00:12:31,967 --> 00:12:33,667
There's Ricardo Jacinto.

291
00:12:35,333 --> 00:12:38,033
It's too dangerous for you
to go out there.

292
00:12:42,200 --> 00:12:43,533
Let this rest.

293
00:12:45,333 --> 00:12:46,933
Stop your people.

294
00:12:51,833 --> 00:12:54,567
Forget about Samantha Jacinto.

295
00:12:55,167 --> 00:12:56,333
She's definitely dead.

296
00:12:57,333 --> 00:13:00,033
She's probably
somewhere composting.

297
00:13:04,767 --> 00:13:07,967
We have a business to run.

298
00:13:09,267 --> 00:13:10,667
[LUCAS SIGHS]

299
00:13:11,667 --> 00:13:14,167
Victor Zafra's father
used to be a cop.

300
00:13:14,167 --> 00:13:16,100
He got dismissed because...

301
00:13:16,100 --> 00:13:18,900
let's just say
because of his misconduct.

302
00:13:18,900 --> 00:13:19,900
And from then on,

303
00:13:21,100 --> 00:13:23,067
he loathes NLEA.

304
00:13:23,067 --> 00:13:25,233
So he's getting back at you
through Sam?

305
00:13:25,233 --> 00:13:27,067
I don't know, Max.

306
00:13:27,067 --> 00:13:29,733
But I'm sure we have to hold
some leverage over them

307
00:13:30,367 --> 00:13:31,867
before they make another move.

308
00:13:31,867 --> 00:13:38,767
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

309
00:13:38,767 --> 00:13:39,900
[MUSIC FADES]

310
00:13:39,900 --> 00:13:42,900
- These should get washed.
- What do you want...

311
00:13:42,900 --> 00:13:44,967
Auntie, what are we going
to cook?

312
00:13:44,967 --> 00:13:46,067
I have eggs here.

313
00:13:46,067 --> 00:13:47,633
But hold on, Gabo.

314
00:13:47,633 --> 00:13:50,367
It's just that
I'm a bit worried.

315
00:13:50,367 --> 00:13:53,633
What if Betchay
suddenly comes home

316
00:13:53,633 --> 00:13:56,200
and almost sees Gloria again?

317
00:13:56,233 --> 00:13:58,967
- I'm nervous.
- She usually comes home at 3.

318
00:13:58,967 --> 00:14:00,767
What if she comes home early?

319
00:14:00,767 --> 00:14:02,733
- [BETCHAY] Rudy!
- See? I told you.

320
00:14:02,733 --> 00:14:04,400
- [BETCHAY] Rudy!
- What now?

321
00:14:04,400 --> 00:14:05,800
Auntie...

322
00:14:05,800 --> 00:14:07,967
I think you might've
summoned her.

323
00:14:07,967 --> 00:14:08,967
Auntie Betchay is home.

324
00:14:08,967 --> 00:14:10,300
- What do we do now?
- Gloria!

325
00:14:10,300 --> 00:14:11,867
- [BETCHAY] Rudy!
- Gloria?

326
00:14:12,667 --> 00:14:14,067
Hey! What are you doing here?

327
00:14:14,067 --> 00:14:15,733
Shhh! Be quiet!

328
00:14:15,733 --> 00:14:16,967
We have a problem.

329
00:14:16,967 --> 00:14:18,033
Auntie Betchay is home.

330
00:14:18,967 --> 00:14:19,933
[WHISPERS] Be quiet!

331
00:14:20,967 --> 00:14:22,767
[MAMENG] Act normal. Act normal.

332
00:14:22,767 --> 00:14:23,933
I'll take care of this.

333
00:14:23,933 --> 00:14:26,000
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

334
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:27,633
- [RUDY] Betchay.
- Hi, Dy!

335
00:14:28,800 --> 00:14:30,433
[GABO BREATHING HEAVILY]

336
00:14:30,433 --> 00:14:31,967
She can't see you.

337
00:14:35,033 --> 00:14:39,167
You can't leave this bathroom,
understand?

338
00:14:39,167 --> 00:14:40,167
Don't make any noise.

339
00:14:40,167 --> 00:14:41,133
Mm-hmm.

340
00:14:43,800 --> 00:14:45,800
Happy birthday!

341
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:48,833
This is my gift for you.

342
00:14:48,833 --> 00:14:50,800
- What's this?
- Open it.

343
00:14:55,033 --> 00:14:59,433
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

344
00:14:59,433 --> 00:15:00,933
That looks expensive.

345
00:15:02,533 --> 00:15:04,467
Of course, it is. I love him.

346
00:15:05,467 --> 00:15:07,267
Where did you get the money?

347
00:15:08,333 --> 00:15:11,333
I'm the manager now.
I get bigger tips.

348
00:15:11,333 --> 00:15:12,367
[CHUCKLES]

349
00:15:12,367 --> 00:15:13,533
Betchay.

350
00:15:13,533 --> 00:15:16,467
You didn't have to.
It's okay if we don't do gifts.

351
00:15:16,467 --> 00:15:18,400
Oh, come on, it's your birthday.

352
00:15:18,400 --> 00:15:20,167
We celebrate it once a year.

353
00:15:20,167 --> 00:15:21,367
It has to be special.

354
00:15:21,367 --> 00:15:22,800
Besides...

355
00:15:23,833 --> 00:15:26,200
I want to make up
for what I said last night.

356
00:15:27,400 --> 00:15:28,833
Thank you.

357
00:15:28,833 --> 00:15:31,867
That's just how married life is.

358
00:15:31,867 --> 00:15:33,967
Sometimes you have
disagreements.

359
00:15:33,967 --> 00:15:36,833
And making up afterward
is what matters.

360
00:15:40,900 --> 00:15:42,033
Thank you, Betchay.

361
00:15:44,900 --> 00:15:46,967
You bought a lot.

362
00:15:48,167 --> 00:15:49,833
- Oh, these?
- Yeah.

363
00:15:49,833 --> 00:15:52,000
It's nothing.
These are, uh, clothes.

364
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:57,100
I wanted to wear something nice
at Rudy's party later.

365
00:15:57,100 --> 00:15:58,900
[BETCHAY CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

366
00:15:58,900 --> 00:16:01,233
- Hold on. Where are you going?
- [MUSIC TURNS PLAYFUL]

367
00:16:01,233 --> 00:16:03,567
- Uh, I need to pee.
- The toilet is clogged.

368
00:16:03,567 --> 00:16:04,933
The toilet is clogged, right?

369
00:16:04,933 --> 00:16:05,833
[RUDY] Yes, it is.

370
00:16:05,833 --> 00:16:08,233
It's always clogged.
I can handle it.

371
00:16:08,267 --> 00:16:09,900
It's really clogged this time.

372
00:16:09,900 --> 00:16:12,033
We'll fix it.
You were up all night, right?

373
00:16:13,067 --> 00:16:14,067
[BETCHAY] Huh?

374
00:16:14,067 --> 00:16:15,400
You need to rest.

375
00:16:15,400 --> 00:16:18,900
He's right, Betchay.
You should rest for now.

376
00:16:18,900 --> 00:16:21,067
We'll tell you
when it's all fixed.

377
00:16:21,067 --> 00:16:23,267
I'm about to burst! Move!

378
00:16:23,267 --> 00:16:24,567
- [DOOR OPENS]
- Aah!

379
00:16:24,567 --> 00:16:25,867
Auntie Betchay!

380
00:16:25,867 --> 00:16:28,933
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

381
00:16:31,533 --> 00:16:32,567
Who is that woman?!
Who is this woman?!

382
00:16:33,200 --> 00:16:34,367
Rudy!

383
00:16:34,367 --> 00:16:37,000
That's why you didn't
want me to go into the bathroom!

384
00:16:37,133 --> 00:16:41,100
Oh! That's why
you were stopping me!

385
00:16:41,300 --> 00:16:43,433
Gabo!
Who the hell is that woman?

386
00:16:43,600 --> 00:16:45,933
What have you done
this time?!

387
00:16:46,100 --> 00:16:48,267
Who is she?!

388
00:16:48,433 --> 00:16:50,967
[SIGHS] Uh...
Mama Betchay.

389
00:16:51,133 --> 00:16:53,767
She's my wife.

390
00:16:53,933 --> 00:16:56,033
H-Her name is Gloria.

391
00:16:56,133 --> 00:16:58,567
Wife?!

392
00:16:58,667 --> 00:17:00,967
Since when did you
have a wife?!

393
00:17:01,133 --> 00:17:03,067
[DANTE] They met in prison.

394
00:17:03,167 --> 00:17:05,733
They got married
in there too.

395
00:17:06,733 --> 00:17:11,367
Jeez, Gabo.
You are unbelievable.

396
00:17:11,500 --> 00:17:13,800
You actually found a wife
in jail?

397
00:17:13,900 --> 00:17:15,800
Wow, Gabo.

398
00:17:15,967 --> 00:17:19,167
Rudy, what do you have to say?

399
00:17:19,433 --> 00:17:21,567
Now that you're making
a bit of money,

400
00:17:21,700 --> 00:17:26,633
you decided to bring in
another mouth to feed?

401
00:17:28,533 --> 00:17:31,167
Don't worry, Mama Betchay.

402
00:17:31,300 --> 00:17:34,933
I promise that
we won't be a burden.

403
00:17:34,933 --> 00:17:37,567
We'll chip in
and help with the chores.

404
00:17:37,800 --> 00:17:39,133
Wait, wait, wait.

405
00:17:39,367 --> 00:17:41,833
You don't have plans
to move out?!

406
00:17:41,833 --> 00:17:43,267
You're already married!

407
00:17:43,467 --> 00:17:45,067
Betchay!

408
00:17:45,200 --> 00:17:47,933
No one is leaving,
no one is moving out!

409
00:17:47,933 --> 00:17:49,600
- Rudy.
- Betchay!

410
00:17:49,800 --> 00:17:50,967
Gabo is my son.

411
00:17:51,333 --> 00:17:52,533
My only son.

412
00:17:52,533 --> 00:17:56,533
He and my future grandchild
will get this house someday.

413
00:17:56,733 --> 00:17:58,200
Future grandchild?
They just got married!

414
00:17:58,367 --> 00:17:59,767
- And--
- Wait a minute!

415
00:17:59,900 --> 00:18:03,000
Am I getting this right?

416
00:18:03,133 --> 00:18:05,533
I have no right
to this house?

417
00:18:05,667 --> 00:18:10,833
If you have a problem with
Gabo and his wife staying here,

418
00:18:10,967 --> 00:18:12,867
let's talk about it.

419
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:15,033
But no one is leaving!

420
00:18:15,167 --> 00:18:22,033
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

421
00:18:24,733 --> 00:18:25,733
[SEBASTIAN CLEARS THROAT]

422
00:18:25,733 --> 00:18:26,900
- Sir?
- Hmm?

423
00:18:27,033 --> 00:18:28,333
We've looked everywhere

424
00:18:28,567 --> 00:18:30,200
within a 1-kilometer radius
of the crime scene.

425
00:18:30,333 --> 00:18:32,367
But we still don't have
a concrete lead.

426
00:18:32,533 --> 00:18:36,033
Then let's expand our search.

427
00:18:36,033 --> 00:18:38,367
[GRUNTS] Well,
of course we won't stop.

428
00:18:38,667 --> 00:18:40,167
We're just getting started.

429
00:18:40,267 --> 00:18:42,367
We're not giving up.

430
00:18:42,533 --> 00:18:44,833
[ROBERT] Wait,
why do you seem happy, sir?

431
00:18:44,933 --> 00:18:46,633
Well, guys,

432
00:18:46,733 --> 00:18:51,500
Sam's family really appreciates
everything we're doing.

433
00:18:51,600 --> 00:18:55,233
[CASTOR] Sir Seb,
we're not after that.

434
00:18:55,433 --> 00:18:59,033
Our goal is to find Ma'am Sam.

435
00:18:59,133 --> 00:19:00,533
Tony.

436
00:19:01,767 --> 00:19:04,167
This is a very important mission
for the agency.

437
00:19:04,267 --> 00:19:07,067
The Jacintos have faith in me.

438
00:19:07,200 --> 00:19:09,433
So we have to do our best

439
00:19:09,600 --> 00:19:13,600
because my future in-laws
are counting on us.

440
00:19:13,767 --> 00:19:14,900
- [CASTOR] Ah...
- [CLEARS THROAT]

441
00:19:15,067 --> 00:19:18,433
[WHIMSICAL MUSIC PLAYING]

442
00:19:18,600 --> 00:19:20,600
- All right, then.
- Sir Seb.

443
00:19:20,767 --> 00:19:24,600
You are the only one
who can lead this search.

444
00:19:24,767 --> 00:19:26,333
Yes, you're right about that.

445
00:19:26,433 --> 00:19:30,100
When it comes to Sam,
I'm your guy.

446
00:19:30,300 --> 00:19:31,467
Am I clear?

447
00:19:32,267 --> 00:19:33,900
- All right?
- They got it.

448
00:19:34,767 --> 00:19:36,200
Mm.

449
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:38,100
[WHIMSICAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

450
00:19:41,400 --> 00:19:42,800
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

451
00:19:42,933 --> 00:19:43,867
Oh.

452
00:19:45,600 --> 00:19:48,233
Why is the NLEA here?

453
00:19:48,400 --> 00:19:51,733
This is Captain Umali,
and this is Colonel Domingo...

454
00:19:51,900 --> 00:19:54,633
- Mm.
- ...Max's chief at the station.

455
00:19:54,767 --> 00:19:58,433
Are you here to give an update
about my daughter?

456
00:20:00,900 --> 00:20:03,767
We are still searching for her.

457
00:20:03,967 --> 00:20:07,633
We're doing everything we can
to find her.

458
00:20:07,800 --> 00:20:10,000
Well, if that's the case,

459
00:20:11,600 --> 00:20:14,233
you won't find her here.

460
00:20:14,333 --> 00:20:16,100
They're here for
a different reason.

461
00:20:18,633 --> 00:20:22,100
- Umali, Colonel, thank you.
- Sir.

462
00:20:22,200 --> 00:20:23,467
Ma'am.

463
00:20:24,867 --> 00:20:26,133
Ma'am.

464
00:20:27,667 --> 00:20:30,233
Ricardo, why are there
NLEA officers in my home?

465
00:20:30,333 --> 00:20:33,467
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

466
00:20:33,633 --> 00:20:35,933
It's about the Zafras.

467
00:20:36,067 --> 00:20:39,033
[MUSIC TURNS TENSE]

468
00:20:39,167 --> 00:20:41,300
Zafras again?!

469
00:20:41,400 --> 00:20:44,100
What's going on
with the Zafras?!

470
00:20:46,333 --> 00:20:47,267
Hmm?

471
00:20:49,800 --> 00:20:51,033
[EXHALES HEAVILY]

472
00:20:51,167 --> 00:20:56,600
The NLEA will assist
in apprehending them.

473
00:20:59,167 --> 00:21:05,967
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

474
00:21:13,400 --> 00:21:14,500
Fine.

475
00:21:17,233 --> 00:21:19,967
It's not like I can do
anything about this.

476
00:21:25,367 --> 00:21:26,467
Is she pregnant?

477
00:21:29,200 --> 00:21:30,567
Not yet.

478
00:21:30,700 --> 00:21:32,067
What's your name again?

479
00:21:34,667 --> 00:21:35,900
It's Gloria, ma'am.

480
00:21:37,233 --> 00:21:38,467
Gloria.

481
00:21:41,600 --> 00:21:45,333
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

482
00:21:45,467 --> 00:21:47,600
Welcome to the family.

483
00:21:54,300 --> 00:21:56,500
I hope you can survive here.

484
00:21:56,600 --> 00:22:04,033
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

485
00:22:06,933 --> 00:22:09,533
[SAM] My situation here
is getting more difficult.

486
00:22:09,633 --> 00:22:11,367
<i> But I have to endure.</i>

487
00:22:11,467 --> 00:22:15,600
<i>I can't leave
until I have solid evidence</i>

488
00:22:15,767 --> 00:22:17,533
<i> against the Zafras.</i>

489
00:22:17,633 --> 00:22:19,867
<i> I also need to stay</i>

490
00:22:19,967 --> 00:22:24,933
<i>and gather evidence
to clear my name.</i>

491
00:22:25,100 --> 00:22:25,900
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

492
00:22:30,467 --> 00:22:31,400
[EXHALES]

493
00:22:32,267 --> 00:22:33,433
Ricardo!

494
00:22:34,167 --> 00:22:36,900
What's going on
with the Zafras?

495
00:22:36,900 --> 00:22:39,567
Why do you keep retaliating
against them?

496
00:22:40,300 --> 00:22:42,500
- Isobel--
- No, I already know.

497
00:22:42,500 --> 00:22:45,433
You're always avoiding
this topic.

498
00:22:45,433 --> 00:22:47,567
You're hiding something from me!

499
00:22:47,567 --> 00:22:50,933
Are the Zafras connected
to everything that's happening?

500
00:22:50,967 --> 00:22:53,133
Do you have a history
with the Zafras?

501
00:22:53,133 --> 00:22:55,600
Are they the reason
why Sam is missing?

502
00:22:56,433 --> 00:22:58,967
I'm just doing this
to get back at them.

503
00:22:58,967 --> 00:22:59,933
[ISOBEL SCOFFS]

504
00:23:00,967 --> 00:23:02,267
To get back at them?

505
00:23:03,967 --> 00:23:07,400
Or to retaliate
against the Zafras?

506
00:23:10,500 --> 00:23:12,167
For what they did to Sam.

507
00:23:12,167 --> 00:23:15,600
Instead of trying to get back
at your enemies,

508
00:23:15,600 --> 00:23:20,333
why don't you prioritize
getting Sam back?

509
00:23:20,333 --> 00:23:22,533
And start thinking of how
you can make up

510
00:23:22,567 --> 00:23:26,600
for your shortcomings
as her father!

511
00:23:31,333 --> 00:23:37,033
[FOOTSTEPS RETREATING]

512
00:23:37,033 --> 00:23:39,967
- I'm sorry. Because of me--
- Love.

513
00:23:41,200 --> 00:23:42,967
You don't have to apologize.

514
00:23:43,533 --> 00:23:45,000
You did nothing wrong.

515
00:23:45,900 --> 00:23:49,167
Just excuse Mama Betchay.
That's just how she is.

516
00:23:49,167 --> 00:23:51,367
S-She didn't mean anything.

517
00:23:52,200 --> 00:23:53,467
It's fine.

518
00:23:53,900 --> 00:23:56,467
[RUDY] Gabo's right.
I'm the head of our family.

519
00:23:57,900 --> 00:24:01,167
I get to decide
who leaves and who stays.

520
00:24:02,033 --> 00:24:03,000
[MAMENG] Gloria...

521
00:24:04,167 --> 00:24:06,167
Now you understand

522
00:24:06,167 --> 00:24:09,233
why we don't want Betchay
to see you.

523
00:24:09,233 --> 00:24:12,200
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

524
00:24:12,200 --> 00:24:13,533
Oh.

525
00:24:13,533 --> 00:24:15,333
Let's stay in the kitchen.

526
00:24:15,333 --> 00:24:18,033
Betchay might wake and hear us.
Come on.

527
00:24:18,567 --> 00:24:19,567
Love...

528
00:24:20,667 --> 00:24:22,000
I'm sorry.

529
00:24:23,367 --> 00:24:25,867
I hope Mama Betchay's words
didn't hurt you.

530
00:24:27,500 --> 00:24:28,500
It's fine.

531
00:24:28,500 --> 00:24:35,533
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

532
00:24:35,567 --> 00:24:36,933
Gabo.

533
00:24:36,933 --> 00:24:38,067
Let's talk outside.

534
00:24:39,633 --> 00:24:42,433
[MAMENG] I'll keep Rudy's watch
for now.

535
00:24:44,400 --> 00:24:45,333
[FABRIC THUMPS]

536
00:24:47,567 --> 00:24:49,067
[DOOR SLAMS]

537
00:24:49,067 --> 00:24:52,100
[RUDY] That woman
really is just something else!

538
00:24:52,100 --> 00:24:54,933
- Yeah.
- She knows we have a visitor!

539
00:24:55,933 --> 00:25:00,600
And yet she's so rude to me!
She keeps belittling us!

540
00:25:02,267 --> 00:25:03,667
My god.

541
00:25:03,667 --> 00:25:05,367
That's why you got me confused.

542
00:25:06,500 --> 00:25:08,333
How did you like Betchay?

543
00:25:08,333 --> 00:25:11,067
You know, Dante,
she wasn't like this before.

544
00:25:12,000 --> 00:25:14,100
Ever since our child died,

545
00:25:14,100 --> 00:25:16,233
she started treating
Gabo differently!

546
00:25:16,233 --> 00:25:19,633
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

547
00:25:19,633 --> 00:25:20,600
Pa.

548
00:25:22,600 --> 00:25:24,067
I think I might be the reason

549
00:25:24,067 --> 00:25:26,400
why Mama Betchay started
treating me differently.

550
00:25:28,733 --> 00:25:30,433
She's blaming me...

551
00:25:32,100 --> 00:25:33,633
...for my sibling's death.

552
00:25:34,667 --> 00:25:36,267
Gabo, it's not like that.

553
00:25:37,467 --> 00:25:38,967
You know...

554
00:25:39,300 --> 00:25:44,600
That's not enough reason
for her to treat us like this!

555
00:25:47,000 --> 00:25:49,600
All I'm worried about is Gloria.

556
00:25:51,133 --> 00:25:54,233
I'm sure Betchay will give her
a hard time.

557
00:25:55,267 --> 00:25:56,267
[RUDY SIGHS]

558
00:25:56,267 --> 00:26:00,467
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

559
00:26:00,467 --> 00:26:02,300
[SAM] Poor Gabo.

560
00:26:03,133 --> 00:26:05,567
<i> His stepmother
treats him harshly.</i>

561
00:26:06,467 --> 00:26:10,600
Now, I'm slowly getting to know
<i> his personality.</i>

562
00:26:11,333 --> 00:26:18,333
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

563
00:26:33,333 --> 00:26:38,767
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

564
00:26:39,133 --> 00:26:43,000
I'll destroy Team Alpha's trust
<i> in each other.</i>

565
00:26:43,167 --> 00:26:46,667
<i>It'll be easier for me
to manipulate the agency</i>

566
00:26:46,833 --> 00:26:49,400
<i> to free Victor Zafra.</i>

567
00:26:49,533 --> 00:26:50,800
<i> This is a raid! Get down!</i>

568
00:26:50,933 --> 00:26:53,133
<i> Ricardo is behind all this!</i>

569
00:26:53,233 --> 00:26:54,033
<i> They want war!</i>

570
00:26:54,233 --> 00:26:56,933
<i> Tell me where
I can find the Jacintos.</i>

571
00:26:56,933 --> 00:26:58,167
<i>I'll kill every single one
of them.</i>

572
00:26:58,333 --> 00:27:00,033
<i> I'll come with you.</i>

573
00:27:00,167 --> 00:27:03,633
<i>Happy birthday!
Happy birthday! Happy birthday!</i>

574
00:27:03,767 --> 00:27:06,900
<i>We brought dessert!
It's black kutsinta!</i>

575
00:27:08,000 --> 00:27:09,467
<i>What are you waiting for?
Go get dressed,</i>

576
00:27:09,567 --> 00:27:11,167
<i> so the fun won't stop!</i>

577
00:27:14,167 --> 00:27:15,900
<i> - There's kutsinta--
</i>- [CONFETTI POPS]

578
00:27:16,967 --> 00:27:23,900
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA"
BY JUAN KARLOS PLAYING]
